
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. THE -3*eps SCALING OF THE COMPTON HEATING RATE (verified, not assumed)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  sigma_T = (8pi/3)(alpha hbar/(m_e c))^2 = 6.652459e-29 m^2
  CODATA sigma_T                          = 6.652459e-29 m^2
  agreement                               = -0.0000 %
  => sigma_T ~ alpha^2 / m_e^2  (both explicit in the expression)

  Gamma_C = (8 sigma_T a_r T_CMB^4)/(3 m_e c) * x_e/(1+f_He+x_e)
          ~ (alpha^2/m_e^2) * (1/m_e) = alpha^2 / m_e^3
  => d ln Gamma_C / d ln m_e = -3  =>  Gamma_C -> Gamma_C*(1+eps)^-3

  the model's own C source agrees, independently:
    source/thermodynamics.c:2612  rescale_rate = alpha*alpha/me/me/me;
    source/thermodynamics.c:2714  rate_gamma_b *= rescale_rate;
    source/thermodynamics.c:91    sigmaTrescale = alpha*alpha/me/me;
    source/thermodynamics.c:3988  rescale_rhs   = alpha^3*me^3   (recombination
                                  RHS -- so x_e is modified too, not held fixed)

  eps = 27*alpha/(5*pi) = 0.012543225  (1.2543 %)
  -3*eps                = -0.037629675  (-3.7630 %)
  exact (1+eps)^-3 - 1  = -0.036705050  (-3.6705 %)

