10. ANSWER
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  SIGN: the modified gas is COLDER at every z below decoupling and the trough
        is DEEPER.  The registered sign HOLDS.

  COMPUTED DEPTH, z = 17, T_s -> T_g:
      +1.03 % deeper  (CLASS thermodynamics, fade edge, the headline number)
      +1.04 % deeper  (CLASS thermodynamics, legacy step edge)
      +1.03 % deeper  (independent ODE, self-consistent x_e)
      +1.18 % deeper  (independent ODE, rate effect only, x_e frozen)

  vs the registered estimate of +4.6 % -> the registry is HIGH by ~4.5x.
  The prediction survives in SIGN and dies in MAGNITUDE: it is a ~1% effect,
  not a ~5% effect.
